0-60",no="Best match per slot for Feral (Tank) by stat priority, picked from dungeon drops, quest rewards and crafting at this level range. Quest and crafted pieces are listed in the sections below.",keys={"druid-g1149","druid-g1232","druid-g1119","druid-g1181","druid-g981","druid-g1245","druid-g1246","druid-g1243","druid-g1033","druid-g1014","druid-g1250","druid-g1044","druid-g108","druid-g71","druid-g1240"}}},title="Feral (Tank) | WoW Forever Druid Field Guide",nav={{id="overview",x=S[727]},{id="journey",x=S[594]},{id="talents",x=S[514]},{id="stats",x=S[622]},{id="combat",x=S[623]},{id="macros",x=S[641]},{id="dungeons",x=S[565]},{id="professions",x=S[595]},{id="crafting",x=S[579]},{id="questgear",x=S[556]},{id=S[507],x=S[671]}},asideNote=S[114],talentString="000000000000000055220302123102115510055",ranks={{tree=S[119],name="Ferocity",r=5,max=5},{tree=S[119],name="Furor",r=5,max=5},{tree=S[119],name=S[674],r=2,max=2},{tree=S[119],name=S[634],r=2,max=3},{tree=S[119],name="Thick Hide",r=3,max=3},{tree=S[119],name="Savage Fury",r=2,max=2},{tree=S[119],name=S[759],r=1,max=1},{tree=S[119],name=S[675],r=2,max=2},{tree=S[119],name=S[645],r=3,max=3},{tree=S[119],name="Lacerate",r=1,max=1},{tree=S[119],name=S[975],r=2,max=2},{tree=S[119],name=S[626],r=1,max=1},{tree=S[119],name=S[658],r=1,max=2},{tree=S[119],name=S[729],r=5,max=5},{tree=S[119],name=S[910],r=5,max=5},{tree=S[119],name="Primal Bite",r=1,max=1},{tree="Restoration",name=S[535],r=5,max=5},{tree="Restoration",name="Naturalist",r=5,max=5}},order={{l1=10,l2=14,tree=S[119],name="Ferocity",r1=1,r2=5,max=5},{l1=15,l2=17,tree=S[119],name="Furor",r1=1,r2=3,max=5},{l1=18,l2=19,tree=S[119],name=S[674],r1=1,r2=2,max=2},{l1=20,l2=20,tree=S[119],name=S[759],r1=1,r2=1,max=1},{l1=21,l2=22,tree=S[119],name="Savage Fury",r1=1,r2=2,max=2},{l1=23,l2=24,tree=S[119],name=S[675],r1=1,r2=2,max=2},{l1=25,l2=25,tree=S[119],name="Lacerate",r1=1,r2=1,max=1},{l1=26,l2=28,tree=S[119],name=S[645],r1=1,r2=3,max=3},{l1=29,l2=29,tree=S[119],name=S[634],r1=1,r2=1,max=3},{l1=30,l2=30,tree=S[119],name=S[626],r1=1,r2=1,max=1},{l1=31,l2=32,tree=S[119],name=S[975],r1=1,r2=2,max=2},{l1=33,l2=33,tree=S[119],name=S[658],r1=1,r2=1,max=2},{l1=34,l2=34,tree=S[119],name=S[634],r1=2,r2=2,max=3},{l1=35,l2=39,tree=S[119],name=S[729],r1=1,r2=5,max=5},{l1=40,l2=40,tree=S[119],name="Primal Bite",r1=1,r2=1,max=1},{l1=41,l2=45,tree="Restoration",name=S[535],r1=1,r2=5,max=5},{l1=46,l2=50,tree="Restoration",name="Naturalist",r1=1,r2=5,max=5},{l1=51,l2=52,tree=S[119],name="Furor",r1=4,r2=5,max=5},{l1=53,l2=55,tree=S[119],name="Thick Hide",r1=1,r2=3,max=3},{l1=56,l2=60,tree=S[119],name=S[910],r1=1,r2=5,max=5}},blocks={{t="anchor",id="overview"},{t="p",s="eyebrow",x=S[558]},{t="h1",x=S[974],sub=S[643]},{t="p",s="lede",x="Bear Form threat with Maul, Swipe, Lacerate and Primal Bite at 40, and Cat Form for questing between dungeons. Bear attacks use your weapon’s damage per second, and Bear Form multiplies the armor on your gear."},{t="pills",list={S[636],"Tank leveling build",S[596]}},{t="anchor",id="journey"},{t="kicker",x=S[728]},{t="h2",x=S[470]},{t="p",x="These stages follow the talent order below. This tank build takes its extra points in Restoration (“Feral Reflection”), which suits most players better than a Balance alternative."},{t="p",s="level",x="10–24 · Rage, speed and Feral Charge"},{t="p",x="Ferocity 5/5 (10–14) lowers the cost of Maul, Swipe and Primal Bite. Furor 3/5 (15–17) gives Rage when you shift into Bear Form. Feral Swiftness 2/2 (18–19), Feral Charge at 20 to reach and interrupt an enemy in Bear Form, Savage Fury 2/2 (21–22) and Sharpened Claws 2/2 (23–24)."},{t="p",s="level",x="25–40 · Lacerate to Primal Bite"},{t="p",x="Lacerate at 25 is a stacking bleed with high threat. Predatory Strikes 3/3 (26–28), Feral Instinct (29 and 34), Leader of the Pack at 30, Blood Frenzy 2/2 (31–32) for 5 Rage on critical strikes, Natural Instinct at 33, Rend and Tear 5/5 (35–39) and Primal Bite at 40."},{t="p",s="level",x="41–60 · Restoration, Rage and armor"},{t="p",x="Heart of the Wild 5/5 (41–45) adds 20% Stamina in Bear Form, Naturalist 5/5 (46–50) raises damage, Furor 5/5 (51–52) gives more Rage when you shift into Bear Form, Thick Hide 3/3 (53–55) adds armor, and Natural Reaction 5/5 (56–60) finishes the build."},{t="anchor",id="talents"},{t="kicker",x=S[515]},{t="h2",x=S[636]},{t="p",x=S[81]},{t="widget",w="talents"},{t="h4",s="summary",x=S[566]},{t="widget",w="ranks"},{t="h4",s="summary",x=S[502]},{t="p",x=S[145]},{t="widget",w="order"},{t="p",s="notice",x="Lacerate keeps the target bleeding, so Rend and Tear applies to your Bear attacks too. Thick Hide and Natural Reaction come last, once your threat tools are in place, to add armor and mitigation."},{t="anchor",id="stats"},{t="kicker",x=S[624]},{t="h2",x=S[541]},{t="p",x="Bear Form multiplies the armor on your gear, so armor and Stamina come first for survival. Your threat comes from damage, so the Cat stats still matter."},{t="h3",x=S[691]},{t="stat",i=1,b="Armor",x="higher-armor leather"},{t="stat",i=2,b="Stamina",x=""},{t="stat",i=3,b="Agility",x="dodge and armor"},{t="stat",i=4,b=S[730],x="two-handers"},{t="stat",i=5,b="Strength",x=""},{t="p",s="small",x="Bear attacks also use your weapon’s damage per second, so keep a strong two-hander."},{t="h3",x="At level 60: survival"},{t="stat",i=1,b="Armor",x=""},{t="stat",i=2,b="Defense",x="to 440"},{t="stat",i=3,b="Stamina",x=""},{t="stat",i=4,b="Agility",x=""},{t="stat",i=5,b="Dodge",x=""},{t="p",s="small",x="Bear tanks cannot become immune to crushing blows, so stacking armor and health matters. Armor reduces physical damage by at most 75%."},{t="h3",x="At level 60: threat"},{t="stat",i=1,b=S[730],x=""},{t="stat",i=2,b="Expertise",x="to 6.5%, up to 14% when tanking"},{t="stat",i=3,b="Hit chance",x="to 8%"},{t="stat",i=4,b="Agility",x=""},{t="stat",i=5,b="Strength",x=""},{t="p",s="small",x="Threat follows damage, so a tank with weak gear can lose enemies to strong damage dealers."},{t="p",s="notice",x="Melee hit cap: 8% for special attacks against raid bosses. Expertise removes dodge at 6.5% and parry at 14% (parry only matters from the front). Defense 440 makes a level 63 boss unable to land a critical hit on you. The level 60 list is an early estimate: the beta stopped at level 30, so expect changes once endgame gear is known. A big upgrade in a lower stat can still beat a small one in a higher stat."},{t="anchor",id="combat"},{t="kicker",x=S[542]},{t="h2",x=S[580]},{t="p",x="Treat this as a priority list. Growl arrives at 10, Swipe at 16, Lacerate (talent) at 25, Frenzied Regeneration at 36, Primal Bite and Dire Bear Form at 40 and Barkskin at 44."},{t="h4",x="Pull"},{t="p",x="Cast Faerie Fire to pull from range; it is free in Bear Form. Use Enrage before the pull for extra Rage, and Feral Charge to reach a caster."},{t="h4",x="Hold threat"},{t="p",x="Keep Demoralizing Roar on the enemies you are tanking and use Primal Bite whenever it is ready. Keep Lacerate stacked on your main target."},{t="h4",x="Spend Rage"},{t="p",x="Swipe when fighting several enemies; Maul is your single-target Rage spender. Maul replaces your next auto-attack, so its real Rage cost is higher than listed."},{t="h4",x="Taunts"},{t="p",x="Growl a loose enemy back; Challenging Roar for several. The mouseover macros below taunt without changing target."},{t="h4",x="Survival"},{t="p",x="Barkskin works in forms from 44; Frenzied Regeneration turns Rage into health. Bash interrupts or stops a dangerous enemy."},{t="h4",x=S[945]},{t="p",x="Cat Form becomes more effective for open-world questing, while Bear Form lets you take the tank role whenever you choose."},{t="abil",names={"Bear Form","Maul","Swipe","Lacerate","Primal Bite","Demoralizing Roar","Growl","Challenging Roar","Enrage","Frenzied Regeneration","Bash","Barkskin"}},{t="h3",x=S[614]},{t="p",x="Tanking gear: armor and Stamina first, then Agility for dodge and armor and Defense against critical hits; Strength, attack power and hit add threat. Expertise is extra valuable for tanking. Bear Form multiplies item armor, so higher-armor leather matters."},{t="p",x="Bear attacks also use your weapon’s damage per second, so the two-handed path is the same as Cat’s, preferring Stamina and Agility on the weapon. Ironforge Greathammer (Hall of Thanes quest) and Hammer of Orgrimmar (Ragefire Chasm quest) are the first strong Feral weapons."},{t="h3",x=S[543]},{t="p",x=S[74]},{t="p",x=S[109]},{t="anchor",id="macros"},{t="kicker",x=S[644]},{t="h2",x=S[455]},{t="p",x=S[76]},{t="p",s="notice",x=S[62]},{t="macro",n=S[581],x=S[224],code=S[213]},{t="macro",n=S[625],x=S[230],code=S[232]},{t="macro",n=S[582],x=S[227],code=S[214]},{t="macro",n=S[597],x=S[225],code=S[222]},{t="macro",n=S[615],x=S[231],code=S[258]},{t="macro",n=S[464],x=S[154],code=S[142]},{t="macro",n=S[492],x=S[173],code=S[393]},{t="macro",n=S[583],x=S[223],code=S[255]},{t="macro",n=S[616],x=S[238],code=S[351]},{t="macro",n="Primal Bite with auto-attack",x="Uses Primal Bite (talent, 40) in Bear or Dire Bear Form and starts auto-attack.",code="#showtooltip Primal Bite\n/startattack [harm,nodead]\n/cast [harm,nodead] Primal Bite"},{t="macro",n="Mouseover Lacerate",x="Lacerates the enemy under your pointer or your target, building threat on a second enemy while auto-attack stays on your target.",code="#showtooltip Lacerate\n/cast [@mouseover,harm,nodead][harm,nodead] Lacerate"},{t="macro",n="Mouseover Growl",x="Taunts the enemy under your pointer or your target in Bear Form without changing target.",code="#showtooltip Growl\n/cast [@mouseover,harm,nodead][harm,nodead] Growl"},{t="macro",n=S[792],x="Charges the enemy under your pointer or your target in Bear Form, interrupting its cast.",code=S[417]},{t="p",s="small",x=S[318]},{t="anchor",id="dungeons"},{t="kicker",x=S[672]},{t="h2",x=S[503]},{t="p",x=S[93]},{t="widget",w="rarity"},{t="p",s="notice",x=S[94]},{t="p",s="notice",x="Feral (Tank) loot selection · 1 November 2026. Leather, jewelry and cloaks with Stamina, Defense, dodge, bonus armor or Agility, and two-handed maces, staves and polearms with Stamina or physical stats. Pieces with only offensive stats (attack power, hit, critical strike or Strength without Stamina) are on the Cat page instead. Cloth, caster gear, mail, plate and shields are left out."},{t="widget",w="loot"},{t="anchor",id="professions"},{t="kicker",x=S[544]},{t="h2",x=S[493]},{t="p",x=S[106]},{t="widget",w="prof"},{t="anchor",id="crafting"},{t="kicker",x=S[567]},{t="h2",x=S[471]},{t="p",x="These are items to compare, not a mandatory shopping list. Brackets are 1–9, 10–19, 20–29, 30–39, 40–49, 50–59 and level 60. They use the item’s equip/use requirement, not crafting skill; items with no level requirement are placed by item level. Druids wear cloth and leather and use staves, maces, daggers, fist weapons and polearms (train polearms at a weapon master); this page shows only the pieces that suit Feral (Tank). Unknown item requirements remain separate. A published recipe does not establish that its trainer, materials or final acquisition path are available in the beta."},{t="widget",w="craft"},{t="anchor",id="questgear"},{t="kicker",x=S[545]},{t="h2",x=S[444]},{t="p",x=S[39]},{t="widget",w="quest"},{t="anchor",id=S[507]},{t="kicker",x=S[673]},{t="h2",x="Your notes"},{t="widget",w="notes"},{t="p",s="small",x=S[123]}}},{id="restoration",name="Restoration",token="RESTO",gearBrackets={{b="Quest rewards",no="Quest rewards that fit this spec's stat priority, sorted by quest level. The tooltip names the quest, its level, the quest giver and the faction. Quest level is not the minimum pickup level.",keys={"st-druid-2","druid-g175","druid-g172","druid-g335","druid-g58","druid-g120","druid-g171","druid-g254","druid-g263","druid-g195","druid-g113","druid-g179","druid-g264","druid-g267","druid-g285","druid-g49","druid-g269","druid-g278","druid-g279","druid-g64","druid-g157","druid-g219","druid-g292","druid-g11","druid-g143","druid-